{"title":"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that each pair of eight tennis players either played exactly one game last week or did not play at all. Each player participated in all but 12 games. How many games were played among the eight players?\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/4182d0d137373171ef9c24b8604cf33715d1d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }10 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }12 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ }14 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }16 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ }18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each player played in all but 12 games, each player played in the same number of games, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.  Since each game was played by 2 players, this means there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a01d2ca0463f3e0db4e52303e8fd216a7873b523.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12\\cdot 8g = 4g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> games played.  However, by the given there were also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b58e0d527ab0373153beffdb28939f6388a848ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> games played.  Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/9729bed33378c3ba8fd2049780e1c450d4680eeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4g = g + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/45740266ee9fd40875d89b86001dc403483eb9be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaaaef6af03550f5432623a9945a2ddaa0924e0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each player participated in all but 12 games. There are \\( \\binom{8}{2} \\) ways to pair up 2 people. This gives 28, but we subtract the 12 other games from each player to get \\( 28 - 12 = 16 \\Rightarrow \\) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888f8f633d5b26e400d23a0b89d03496ca1c481d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D). 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"32\" /> games.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<hr />\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_20\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 20\">Previous Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_22\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 22\">Next Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam\">Back to Exam</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018113202\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 46/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1569/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3439:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018113202 and revision id 259854. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}